<BaseLayout title="AWS architecture and selected work — Mark Gingrass" description="AWS solutions architecture, FDA research-system modernization, and accountable AI leadership by Mark Gingrass.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">AWS architecture / mission systems / delivery</p>
    <h1>Architecture is a set of decisions I can defend.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I work from the workload outward: access, data, compute, delivery, operations, and the people who will run it. The selected work below shows how that judgment connects to product and federal program leadership.</p>
  </header>

  <AwsArchitecture id="aws-approach" />

  <section class="section fda-lead" id="applied-ai" aria-labelledby="fda-title">
    <div class="shell case-grid">
      <div class="case-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Leading AI in government / FDA</p>
        <h2 id="fda-title">Paving the way for AI in FDA research tracking.</h2>
        <p class="lead-statement">I’m leading FDA’s first research tracking system integrated with AI. Program management, team leadership, stakeholder alignment, and technical direction sit together in my role.</p>
        <p>At the Center for Tobacco Products, I’m moving that work forward inside the agency boundary. The AI checks research abstracts against the governing coding manual, returns supporting evidence, and flags disagreements. FDA reviewers make the final call.</p>
        <p>I use Lean thinking to target the manual comparison work. The system returns recommendations, evidence, and discrepancy flags so regulatory scientists can focus on the cases that need their judgment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="case-steps">
        <div class="case-step"><span>01</span><div><h3>Lead the program.</h3><p>Set priorities, coordinate teams and vendors, and keep delivery tied to the mission.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>02</span><div><h3>Manage the stakeholders.</h3><p>Bring scientific, business, and technical needs into the same decision. Work through disagreements and keep people moving.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>03</span><div><h3>Shape the architecture.</h3><p>Fit AI into the existing research workflow and agency boundary. Require evidence. Keep decision authority with reviewers.</p></div></div>
        <div class="case-step"><span>04</span><div><h3>Connect funding to delivery.</h3><p>Connect investment and acquisition decisions to scope, ownership, and work the teams can execute.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

